  "scope": "Functional current-overlay volume existence check and source-derived Ordinary refusal. Existing child-overlay value cannot disappear through modeled note reshape V/NV framing. Whole Ordinary raw execution returns no successful cache regardless of reshape outcome, source availability or read availability; enclosing delivery rejects an existing parent entry and preserves original parent/queue. No successful reshape, desired current spent flag or desired rollback premise. Native Rust/store/key/clone/tree correspondence and full Transfer remain open. All four executable definitions and original refusal contracts are unchanged from the rejected attempt; the successor adds a small volume-tail lemma and stages rewrite observations before unfolding callback aliases. No successful reshape, desired read flag or rollback cache is a premise. Read errors remain distinct from absence and any present bytes imply spent. Original failed Lean and pre-admission invalid CLI receive zero credit.",
